1
00:00:04,652 --> 00:00:08,633
Welcome to the NEWL AFRICA
Digital System Training programme.

2
00:00:09,685 --> 00:00:12,774
In this first lesson, we'll
look at the bigger picture:

3
00:00:12,784 --> 00:00:15,977
what the management
platform is, why it exists,

4
00:00:15,987 --> 00:00:18,783
and how it supports everyone
in the organisation.

5
00:00:20,752 --> 00:00:24,375
NEWL AFRICA delivers project
work across many sites,

6
00:00:24,385 --> 00:00:28,066
with team leaders in the field
and decision-makers in the office.

7
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:32,247
Without a shared system,
the important details

8
00:00:32,257 --> 00:00:36,088
— who is responsible for a
project, which workers are on site,

9
00:00:36,098 --> 00:00:39,122
what was done today, and
how much has been spent

10
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:43,308
— end up scattered across phone
calls, messages and spreadsheets.

11
00:00:44,352 --> 00:00:49,440
The NEWL AFRICA management platform brings
that information together in one place.

12
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:56,668
Its own tagline sums it up: projects,
teams, daily logs and financials — unified.

13
00:00:58,319 --> 00:01:02,619
For the Board and project owners,
the platform provides visibility:

14
00:01:02,629 --> 00:01:07,443
a consolidated view of projects,
budgets, spending and activity.

15
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,567
For administrators, it provides control.

16
00:01:12,068 --> 00:01:15,170
Projects are created,
team leaders are assigned,

17
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:19,434
and additional fund requests are
reviewed and then approved or declined.

18
00:01:20,485 --> 00:01:24,577
And for team leaders, it
provides a clear, simple routine:

19
00:01:24,587 --> 00:01:28,366
record the casual workers
on site, submit a daily log,

20
00:01:28,376 --> 00:01:31,667
and request additional funds
when they are genuinely needed.

21
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:36,680
Every one of these actions is recorded,
which creates a dependable trail of

22
00:01:36,690 --> 00:01:37,975
accountability.

23
00:01:39,619 --> 00:01:43,053
It's important to understand
how the system is organised.

24
00:01:43,553 --> 00:01:48,277
The platform has two sign-in roles:
the Administrator and the Team Leader.

25
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:52,063
Administrators manage the whole platform.

26
00:01:52,563 --> 00:01:57,007
They create projects, set budgets,
add and assign team leaders,

27
00:01:57,017 --> 00:02:02,215
record expenditure, review fund requests,
approve completed projects and configure

28
00:02:02,225 --> 00:02:04,253
SMS notifications.

29
00:02:05,319 --> 00:02:08,402
Team leaders work on the
projects assigned to them.

30
00:02:08,902 --> 00:02:13,970
They add casual workers, submit
daily logs, request additional funds,

31
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:17,362
and mark their projects as
complete when the work is done.

32
00:02:18,385 --> 00:02:20,790
Casual workers do not sign in.

33
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:25,513
They are recorded by their team leader,
and they can receive an SMS when they are

34
00:02:25,523 --> 00:02:28,527
added to, or removed from, a project.

35
00:02:29,585 --> 00:02:34,165
Board members and project owners do not
have a separate role in the current system.

36
00:02:34,665 --> 00:02:37,767
Their oversight comes through
the administrator's dashboard,

37
00:02:37,777 --> 00:02:42,246
the financial reports and the audit trail,
which administrators can present and walk

38
00:02:42,256 --> 00:02:43,356
through with them.

39
00:02:44,852 --> 00:02:46,788
Let's open the application.

40
00:02:47,289 --> 00:02:49,851
Everything begins at the sign-in screen.

41
00:02:50,885 --> 00:02:54,104
At the top, you'll see
the NEWL AFRICA identity,

42
00:02:54,114 --> 00:02:57,561
followed by two tabs: Admin and Team Leader.

43
00:02:58,062 --> 00:03:00,493
Choose the tab that matches your role.

44
00:03:01,552 --> 00:03:04,244
Team leaders select the Team Leader tab.

45
00:03:04,744 --> 00:03:07,436
Administrators stay on the Admin tab.

46
00:03:08,485 --> 00:03:10,825
Enter your username and password.

47
00:03:11,326 --> 00:03:14,571
Team leader usernames are
created by the administrator,

48
00:03:14,581 --> 00:03:19,174
and the system turns them into a
sign-in address ending in @newl.africa.

49
00:03:19,672 --> 00:03:22,429
You can also type a full email address.

50
00:03:23,452 --> 00:03:27,544
When you select Sign In, the platform
checks your credentials with Firebase

51
00:03:27,554 --> 00:03:31,704
Authentication — a secure sign-in
service provided by Google.

52
00:03:32,752 --> 00:03:37,071
It then confirms that your account
profile matches the tab you selected.

53
00:03:37,572 --> 00:03:40,817
An administrator can't sign in
through the Team Leader tab,

54
00:03:40,827 --> 00:03:44,052
and a team leader can't
sign in as an administrator.

55
00:03:45,085 --> 00:03:49,730
Keep your password private, and never
share your sign-in details with anyone.

56
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:54,237
If you're using a shared computer,
always sign out when you've finished.

57
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:59,587
After signing in, administrators
arrive on the Home dashboard

58
00:03:59,597 --> 00:04:01,651
— the platform's control centre.

59
00:04:02,685 --> 00:04:06,998
At the top, a short summary tells
you how many projects are active,

60
00:04:07,008 --> 00:04:11,770
how many team leaders are registered,
and how many casual workers are on duty.

61
00:04:12,819 --> 00:04:17,203
Below it, four summary cards give you
the essential figures at a glance.

62
00:04:17,704 --> 00:04:22,180
Projects shows the total number of
projects, and how many are active.

63
00:04:23,219 --> 00:04:26,386
Total Budget is the combined
budget of every project,

64
00:04:26,396 --> 00:04:28,736
with the amount spent shown underneath.

65
00:04:29,785 --> 00:04:33,486
Remaining is what's left
after all outflow — that is,

66
00:04:33,496 --> 00:04:36,774
recorded expenditure and
approved additional funds.

67
00:04:37,274 --> 00:04:41,307
And Unread shows how many of your
notifications you haven't opened yet.

68
00:04:42,352 --> 00:04:46,639
On the left, Active Projects lists
projects that are in progress or awaiting

69
00:04:46,649 --> 00:04:50,102
approval, with their SMP
reference, team leader,

70
00:04:50,112 --> 00:04:53,455
status, a progress bar
and the remaining budget.

71
00:04:54,485 --> 00:04:59,058
On the right, Recent Activity shows
the latest actions taken in the system:

72
00:04:59,068 --> 00:05:00,862
who did what, and when.

73
00:05:01,919 --> 00:05:05,867
And when something needs your decision
— such as a pending fund request,

74
00:05:05,877 --> 00:05:10,073
or a project awaiting approval — a
Needs your attention banner appears,

75
00:05:10,083 --> 00:05:12,618
with a Review button that
takes you straight to it.

76
00:05:14,019 --> 00:05:17,518
The sidebar on the left is how
you move around the platform.

77
00:05:18,019 --> 00:05:20,567
Administrators see nine areas.

78
00:05:21,619 --> 00:05:27,006
Home is the dashboard you've just seen, and
Projects holds the full project portfolio.

79
00:05:28,052 --> 00:05:30,659
Team Leaders is where
field leaders are added,

80
00:05:30,669 --> 00:05:32,397
assigned and supported.

81
00:05:32,898 --> 00:05:37,647
Financials brings together budgets,
expenditure and fund requests.

82
00:05:38,685 --> 00:05:43,597
Daily Logs shows every field report,
and All Casuals lists the casual workers

83
00:05:43,607 --> 00:05:45,530
recorded on each project.

84
00:05:46,585 --> 00:05:51,705
Notifications holds your in-app alerts,
the Audit Log keeps a history of actions,

85
00:05:51,715 --> 00:05:55,800
and Settings contains your
profile and the SMS configuration.

86
00:05:56,819 --> 00:06:01,861
At the top of every page, the search bar
lets you quickly find projects by name,

87
00:06:01,871 --> 00:06:05,383
SMP, PO number or module package.

88
00:06:05,884 --> 00:06:08,862
The bell icon opens your notifications.

89
00:06:09,885 --> 00:06:12,818
Your name and role appear at
the bottom of the sidebar,

90
00:06:12,828 --> 00:06:14,647
next to the sign-out button.

91
00:06:16,052 --> 00:06:19,577
Team leaders see a
simpler, focused workspace.

92
00:06:20,619 --> 00:06:24,125
Their sidebar contains
six areas: My Projects,

93
00:06:24,135 --> 00:06:29,652
My Casuals, Daily Logs, Fund
Requests, Notifications and Settings.

94
00:06:30,685 --> 00:06:34,034
Their home page shows only
the projects assigned to them,

95
00:06:34,044 --> 00:06:37,980
along with the casual workers on their
sites, the logs they've submitted,

96
00:06:37,990 --> 00:06:40,252
and their unread notifications.

97
00:06:41,285 --> 00:06:44,348
Team leaders don't see other
team leaders' projects,

98
00:06:44,358 --> 00:06:48,443
the organisation-wide financial
overview, or the audit log.

99
00:06:48,943 --> 00:06:51,909
Those views are reserved for administrators.

100
00:06:53,452 --> 00:06:56,378
Here's how information
moves through the platform.

101
00:06:57,419 --> 00:07:02,312
An administrator creates a project, sets
its budget and assigns a team leader.

102
00:07:03,352 --> 00:07:09,058
The team leader receives an SMS, signs
in, records the casual workers on site,

103
00:07:09,068 --> 00:07:11,070
and submits daily logs.

104
00:07:12,119 --> 00:07:16,152
Every submission is stored
centrally in a Firestore database.

105
00:07:16,652 --> 00:07:20,926
Administrators receive notifications,
and the records become available on the

106
00:07:20,936 --> 00:07:24,761
dashboard, in the financial
reports and in the audit log.

107
00:07:25,785 --> 00:07:28,770
The Board and project owners
can then receive accurate,

108
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,192
up-to-date information
through the administrator,

109
00:07:31,202 --> 00:07:33,659
without chasing updates from the field.

110
00:07:35,519 --> 00:07:40,147
Let's recap. The NEWL AFRICA
platform brings projects,

111
00:07:40,157 --> 00:07:44,593
teams, daily logs and financials
together in one secure place.

112
00:07:45,652 --> 00:07:49,418
There are two sign-in roles,
Administrator and Team Leader,

113
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:52,029
and every important action leaves a record.

114
00:07:53,085 --> 00:07:57,307
In the next lesson, we'll create a
project, add a team leader and assign

115
00:07:57,317 --> 00:08:00,766
responsibility. Thank you for watching.

116
00:08:03,685 --> 00:08:07,705
This training experience was
produced by KEYPOLE TECHNOLOGIES.
